  "prompt": "You are a senior associate on the consumer staples research team at a large asset management firm. The portfolio manager for your firm's large-cap dividend strategy has asked for an investment memo on The Coca-Cola Company (KO) to evaluate whether to initiate or increase a position. The memo must synthesize the attached financial data and recent filing activity to address KO's investment merits and risks, with particular attention to profitability, growth trajectory, and capital efficiency.\n\nMaterials provided:\n1. KO Financial Data Package — contains quarterly and annual XBRL-sourced financial metrics for The Coca-Cola Company including revenue, gross profit, operating income, net income, EPS, total assets, stockholders' equity, cash balances, COGS, and SG&A for the periods Q1 2026, FY 2025, Q3 2025, and Q2 2025.\n2. Recent Filing Activity — a list of recent SEC filings by date, including 10-Q, 8-K, and Form 144 submissions.\n\nTask requirements:\n1. Executive Summary (1 page): Provide a clear investment recommendation (buy/hold/sell) with a 2–3 sentence thesis. Identify KO's ticker, sector classification, and the date of the most recent quarterly data.\n2. Financial Performance Analysis: Analyze revenue trends across the available quarters. Calculate and discuss gross margin and operating margin for Q1 2026 and FY 2025. Compute year-over-year revenue growth where possible from the data provided. Comment on the trend in diluted EPS.\n3. Balance Sheet & Capital Efficiency: Assess total assets, stockholders' equity, and cash position as of Q1 2026. Calculate and interpret return on equity (ROE) using FY 2025 net income and the average of FY 2025 and Q3 2025 stockholders' equity. Discuss any notable shifts in the balance sheet.\n4. Risk Factors: Identify at least three specific risks facing the company, drawing on the financial data trends and the nature of the consumer staples sector. At least one risk must relate to cost pressures or margin compression.\n5. Conclusion & Recommendation: Restate the investment thesis and specify a position sizing suggestion relative to a benchmark-weighted portfolio.\n\nFormatting instructions:\n- Submit as a single PDF document titled 'Investment Memo - The Coca-Cola Company'.\n- Use numbered section headings matching the five sections above.\n- Include an executive summary on the first page.\n- Total length should be 4–6 pages.\n- All financial figures must be cited in billions of dollars with one decimal place (e.g., $47.9B) unless discussing per-share metrics.",
